# HARD RULES (P0)

## 1) 1 CMD = 1 OUTPUT BLOCK (ABSOLUTE)
- For every command I run, I will post exactly ONE code-fence block with ONLY the raw stdout of that command.
- NEVER paste the command text into the block.
- NEVER paste the prompt prefix (e.g. `PS C:\...>`).
- NEVER mix outputs from multiple commands in one block.

## 2) "SLEPENE RADKY" is ONLY if:
- A single block contains evidence of multiple commands OR prompt text.
- Or: the output truly lacks CR/LF separators in the captured raw stdout (not UI wrap).

## 3) NO DANGEROUS REDIRECTION / FALSE ERRORS
- In PowerShell, DO NOT use `2>nul` (cmd syntax) and DO NOT use pipes that trigger Out-File device errors.
- Use PowerShell-native: `2>$null` and `Select-String -Quiet` when possible.

## 4) BAN: dollar-dot
- Never use dollar-dot (e.g. Path, LineNumber on `$`) in scripts or output formatting.
- Use ONLY `$_` (pipeline variable) or explicit named variables.

## 5) Prefer "boolean gates" (Quiet) to avoid formatting issues
- For gates that only need PASS/FAIL, use `Select-String -Quiet` and print PASS/FAIL explicitly.
- Do not print matched lines unless the gate requires audit output.

## 6) If audit output is required:
- Print EXACTLY 1 line per match using a single Write-Output per match, from pipeline objects.
- Example pattern:
  `... | ForEach-Object { Write-Output ($_.Path + ':' + $_.LineNumber + ':' + $_.Line.Trim()) }`
